/*2496. Maximum Value of a String in an Array
The value of an alphanumeric string can be defined as:

The numeric representation of the string in base 10, if it comprises of digits only.
The length of the string, otherwise.
Given an array strs of alphanumeric strings, return the maximum value of any string in 
strs.

Example 1:
Input: strs = ["alic3","bob","3","4","00000"]
Output: 5
Explanation: 
- "alic3" consists of both letters and digits, so its value is its length, i.e. 5.
- "bob" consists only of letters, so its value is also its length, i.e. 3.
- "3" consists only of digits, so its value is its numeric equivalent, i.e. 3.
- "4" also consists only of digits, so its value is 4.
- "00000" consists only of digits, so its value is 0.
Hence, the maximum value is 5, of "alic3".

Example 2:
Input: strs = ["1","01","001","0001"]
Output: 1
Explanation: 
Each string in the array has value 1. Hence, we return 1.


case=1
input=
alic3,bob,3,4,00000
output=
5

case=2
input=
1,01,001,0001
output=
1

case=3
input=
9,99,999,10000,000000
output=
10000


case=4
input=
a,ab,abc,12,1234,00123
output=
1234
*/
import java.util.*;
class MaximumValueofaStringinanArray
{
    public static int maximumValue(String[] strs)
     {
        int maxValue = 0;

        // Traverse each string in the array
        for (String s : strs) 
        {
            int value = 0;
            boolean isNumber = true;

            // Check if the string contains only digits
            for (char ch : s.toCharArray()) 
            {
                if (!Character.isDigit(ch)) 
                {
                    isNumber = false;
                    break;
                }
            }

            // If it contains only digits, convert it to integer
            if (isNumber) {
                value = Integer.parseInt(s);
            } 
            else
             {
                // Otherwise, take the length of the string
                value = s.length();
            }

            // Update the maximum value
            maxValue = Math.max(maxValue, value);
        }

        return maxValue;
    }

    public static void main(String args[])
    {
        Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);
        String s[]=sc.nextLine().split(",");;
        System.out.println(maximumValue(s));
    }
}

